util/os_drm: system calls on DRM files through libdrm when it says so

RADV opens DRM nodes, stats them, maps DRM files and issues requests with
the system calls. mac_linuxgpu's libdrm hands out DRM files of a driver
that runs outside the kernel: the descriptors are sockets of the process
(close, dup and fcntl work on them), but open by path, stat, mmap and
ioctl cannot reach the driver. That libdrm defines LIBDRM_FILE_OPS and
provides drmFileOpen, drmFileStat, drmFileMmap, drmFileMunmap and
drmIoctl for them.

- util/os_drm.h: drm_ioctl uses drmIoctl under LIBDRM_FILE_OPS; new
  os_drm_open, os_drm_stat, os_drm_mmap and os_drm_munmap wrap the system
  calls or the libdrm functions.
- RADV: open and stat render nodes, and map and unmap buffers, with them.
  Without LIBDRM_FILE_OPS the code is unchanged.

